---
import EditorialLayout from '../layouts/EditorialLayout.astro';
import ActionIcon from '../components/editorial/ActionIcon.astro';
import Evidence from '../components/editorial/Evidence.astro';
import Capabilities from '../components/editorial/Capabilities.astro';
import TechStack from '../components/editorial/TechStack.astro';
import CareerTimeline from '../components/editorial/CareerTimeline.astro';
import { profile, mailto, supportingWork, testimonials } from '../content/editorial.js';
const caseUrl = (id) => `/case-studies/${id}/`;
const recommendations = [testimonials[1], testimonials[0], testimonials[2]];
---
<EditorialLayout home>
  <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="intro-title">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <h1 id="intro-title">I’m Andrew.<br />I like knowing<br /><span>what happens next.</span></h1>
      <p class="intro">Someone clicks an ad. Then what? That curiosity has followed me from agency accounts to in-house marketing—and shapes how I work as a paid media specialist.</p>
      <p class="hero-detail">I get hands-on in the account, connect the campaign to the customer, and help the team decide where the next dollar belongs.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href={mailto}>Email Me <ActionIcon name="arrow" /></a><a class="text-link" href={profile.resume} target="_blank" rel="noopener"><ActionIcon name="file" />View résumé</a></div>
      <p class="availability">Open to roles in Greater Vancouver & remote within Canada</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="portrait-block"><img src="/images/andrew-fonseka-480.webp" srcset="/images/andrew-fonseka-480.webp 480w, /images/andrew-fonseka-720.webp 720w" sizes="(max-width: 380px) calc(100vw - 32px), (max-width: 760px) 300px, (max-width: 1000px) 28vw, 360px" width="480" height="480" alt="Andrew Fonseka, Paid Media Specialist" fetchpriority="high" /><figcaption><strong>Andrew Fonseka</strong><span>Agency experience. In-house perspective.</span><span>Greater Vancouver, BC</span></figcaption></figure>
  </section>
  <div class="proof-strip proof-strip--budget wrap" aria-label="Advertising budget and selected campaign outcomes">
    <a href={caseUrl('aegon')}><strong>Seven-figure</strong><span>annual ad budget<small>Aegon · managed with the team</small></span></a>
    <a href={caseUrl('university')}><strong>312</strong><span>fee-paid enrolments<small>Private university · CRM-matched</small></span></a>
    <a href={caseUrl('panasia')}><strong>259</strong><span>funded loans<small>Pan Asia Bank · client-reported</small></span></a>
    <a href={caseUrl('petmart')}><strong>4:1</strong><span>first-order ROAS<small>Petmart.lk · client-reported</small></span></a>
  </div>
  <section id="work" class="selected section wrap">
    <div class="section-heading work-heading"><h2>The work that<br /><span>shaped my thinking.</span></h2><p>Different businesses. Different decisions. Here’s what I worked on, why I took that approach, and what the results tell us.</p></div>
    <article class="featured">
      <div class="featured-copy">
        <div class="case-meta"><span>Private university, Saudi Arabia</span><span>May–Aug 2026</span></div>
        <h3>Two colleges needed students.<br /><span>They needed their own plan.</span></h3>
        <p>A broad campaign was bringing in enquiries. The more useful question was where those students enrolled. Two colleges still needed attention, so I recommended a dedicated Meta campaign and budget.</p>
        <div class="feature-result"><strong>125</strong><span>fee-paid enrolments for the priority colleges<small>Within 312 enrolments across all campaigns</small></span></div>
        <p class="ownership"><strong>My part:</strong> strategy, campaign setup, audiences and a higher-intent lead form. The partner agency ran day-to-day optimisation; the university matched enrolments in its CRM.</p>
        <a class="case-button" href={caseUrl('university')} aria-label="Read the case study: Private university">Read the case study <ActionIcon name="arrow" /></a>
      </div>
      <Evidence />
    </article>
    <div class="supporting-work">
      <h3>A few more chapters</h3>
      <div class="case-grid">{supportingWork.map(c=><article class="case-card"><div class="case-card-top"><h4>{c.name}</h4><span class="tag">{c.context}</span></div><h5>{c.title}</h5><p>{c.body}</p><div class="card-result"><strong>{c.outcome}</strong><span>{c.qualifier}</span></div><a class="case-button" href={caseUrl(c.id)} aria-label={`Read the case study: ${c.name}`}>Read the case study <ActionIcon name="arrow" /></a></article>)}</div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <Capabilities />
  <TechStack />
  <section id="about" class="about section wrap">
    <div class="about-introduction">
      <div class="section-heading"><h2>I get curious.<br /><span>Then I get to work.</span></h2></div>
      <div class="about-body">
        <p class="about-lead">I got my start in agency teams at Enfection and Kites Global, getting into accounts, building campaigns and figuring out what to test next. What keeps me interested is where that work leads: the person behind an enquiry, the decision behind a purchase, and what we can learn from both.</p>
        <p>Moving in-house at Aegon gave me a wider view. A campaign had to connect with product teams, tracking and compliance. I enjoyed joining those pieces up, and that experience strengthened the way I think about a budget: with a founder’s care for what it costs to win a customer, what that customer is worth and where the next dollar should go.</p>
        <p>I brought that perspective into independent education projects, where the questions became very concrete. Which colleges needed students? Which enquiries were ready for an admissions conversation? Helping turn those questions into campaign decisions is the work that energizes me. There’s always something to investigate, a better test to run or a clearer way to explain what the numbers mean.</p>
        <p>That’s what I want to bring to my next team: curiosity, hands-on paid media experience and the enthusiasm to see the work through. I’ll get into the account, share what I’m learning and help you decide what to do next. If you’re hiring in Greater Vancouver or remotely within Canada, I’d love to hear what you’re building.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href={profile.resume} target="_blank" rel="noopener"><ActionIcon name="file" />View my experience</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <CareerTimeline />
  </section>
  <section class="recommendations section wrap" aria-labelledby="recommendations-title">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><h2 id="recommendations-title">The people alongside<br /><span>the work.</span></h2><p>The people I’ve learned from and worked with are part of this story too. Here’s how three of them describe the experience.</p></div><a class="text-link" href={`${profile.linkedin}details/recommendations/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">View on LinkedIn <ActionIcon name="arrow" /></a></div>
    <div class="recommendation-grid">{recommendations.map((t,i)=><figure class:list={["recommendation-card", {"recommendation-featured": i === 0}]}>
      <svg class="quote-mark" width="32" height="26" viewBox="0 0 32 26" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 15C0 7 4 2 12 0v5C7 7 6 10 6 13h7v13H0V15Zm19 0C19 7 23 2 31 0v5c-5 2-6 5-6 8h7v13H19V15Z" /></svg>
      <blockquote><p>“{t.excerpt}”</p></blockquote>
      <figcaption><span class="recommendation-initials" aria-hidden="true">{t.initials}</span><div><strong>{t.name}</strong><span>{t.role}</span></div></figcaption>
      <details><summary>Read the full recommendation</summary><p>“{t.quote}”</p></details>
    </figure>)}</div>
  </section>
</EditorialLayout>

<style is:global>
.editorial .proof-strip--budget { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:0; padding-block:32px; }
.editorial .proof-strip--budget a { display:flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:flex-start; justify-content:flex-start; gap:14px; min-width:0; padding:0 24px; border:0; border-right:1px solid var(--line); }
.editorial .proof-strip--budget a:first-child { padding-left:0; }
.editorial .proof-strip--budget a:last-child { padding-right:0; border-right:0; }
.editorial .proof-strip--budget strong { display:block; font-size:clamp(28px,2.75vw,40px); line-height:1.2; white-space:nowrap; }
.editorial .proof-strip--budget span { display:block; font-size:16px; line-height:1.5; }
.editorial .proof-strip--budget small { display:block; font-size:12px; line-height:1.6; margin-top:6px; }
@media(max-width:1100px) and (min-width:761px) {
 .editorial .proof-strip--budget { grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); padding-block:0; }
 .editorial .proof-strip--budget a { padding:24px; border:0; }
 .editorial .proof-strip--budget a:nth-child(odd) { padding-left:0; border-right:1px solid var(--line); }
 .editorial .proof-strip--budget a:nth-child(-n+2) { border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); }
 .editorial .proof-strip--budget strong { font-size:38px; }
}
@media(max-width:760px) {
 .editorial .proof-strip--budget { grid-template-columns:1fr; padding-block:0; }
 .editorial .proof-strip--budget a, .editorial .proof-strip--budget a:first-child, .editorial .proof-strip--budget a:last-child { display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:8px; padding:24px 0; border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); }
 .editorial .proof-strip--budget a:last-child { border-bottom:0; }
 .editorial .proof-strip--budget strong { font-size:38px; }
}
</style>
